{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "048D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nR' = X' \\times_X R \\ar[dd] \\ar[rr] \\ar[rd] & &\nX' \\times_X U = U' \\ar'[d][dd] \\ar[rd] \\\\\n& R \\ar[dd] \\ar[rr] & & U \\ar[dd] \\\\\nU' = X' \\times_X U \\ar'[r][rr] \\ar[rd] & & X' \\ar[rd] \\\\\n& U \\ar[rr] & & X\n}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9cc2325750c099420a0e28713a1f92d0629c655cffa70a9df3dfa62763e9dc70", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c31e206d6ce7e30f8a50dad1431cae2e8e2d1a5409a4b2a2dbe3499a1d84097", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: Functorial point of view combined with the picture:\n<MATH_0001>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1dc1c79679341b1df38f1d6a34ab83fdeec883269394ee38c98544a6d25a9f98", "unit_id": "tag:048G:proof"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "048D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j' : R' \\to U' \\times_B U'$", "MATH_0002": "$j$", "MATH_0003": "$X'$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-on-invariant}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-base-change}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6568268573e9448e208dcb1c520da2c9c658a3d6b0136df384a5f8ccced3aada", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fdc925f316fc011afe9356402aaa6ea203e3a4f1f07265d5ce084fc634c1e08c", "source_text": "In the situation of Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe call <MATH_0001> the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>base change<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of the pre-relation\n<MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003>. We say it is a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>flat base change<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0004> is a flat\nmorphism of algebraic spaces.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f00364874d1b11603da9977c763172f9cff9f32f5657dcf61526e364784a29c9", "unit_id": "tag:048H:statement"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048D", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2bbc0448955254e6f7d1c398b1fcec2e300a4fdf816d4f3dff9da1630f81d9b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis kind of base change interacts well with taking quotient sheaves\nand quotient stacks.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:34571b8f2f6cae124faa7efd50b703e7c2047aef7075fe3b4fb687df9969c3b0", "unit_id": "tag:048D:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "048D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\nU'/R' = X' \\times_X U/R\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-on-invariant}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-section-quotient-sheaves}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-quotient-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0653d7de603911c37b1a614359624036cee9c3e6ac732cf0715f0bd0d003d1fa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de33e6b6ab990f6026ea20eadf379a99d9fd2e71762ee410c950774203dbefd4", "source_text": "In the situation of Lemma <REF_0001>\nthere is an isomorphism of sheaves\n<MATH_0001>\nFor the construction of quotient sheaves, see\nGroupoids in Spaces, Section <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3200d90bd83d301ed8063e1a6e013514671cd9ba63a34b594bfdd6bfd260795e", "unit_id": "tag:0DTF:statement"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "048D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$U/R$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nR \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] &\nU \\ar[r] &\nU/R\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh$", "MATH_0007": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Sh/X$", "MATH_0009": "$X' \\times_X - : \\Sh/X \\to \\Sh/X'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d7291d21358c782d2ff23a4443b0802cf049592c0303026a307b4c790816d892", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:94b5d31d90ba6f20f9e78cd787e5ddfb9e4afbfd111ba538e57f0aabb20cdcde", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001> is <MATH_0002>-invariant, it is clear that the map\n<MATH_0003> factors through the quotient sheaf <MATH_0004>.\nRecall that by definition\n<MATH_0005>\nis a coequalizer diagram in the category <MATH_0006> of sheaves of sets on\n<MATH_0007>. In fact, this is a coequalizer diagram in the\ncomma category <MATH_0008>. Since the base change functor\n<MATH_0009> is exact (true in any topos),\nwe conclude.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11a107806754b4b3e3d3c0c4d5da7cb3228d4fdceef72e8fc8d7e6911884e622", "unit_id": "tag:0DTF:proof"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "048D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "MATH_0008": "$B$", "MATH_0009": "$g : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0010": "$B$", "MATH_0011": "$(U', R', s', t', c')$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n[U'/R'] \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & [U/R] \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{S}_{X'} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{S}_X\n}\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$2$", "MATH_0014": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-on-invariant}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-section-stacks}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-quotient-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b500571088aece346c1bb28ee3e3164943c3430dc903057803feb146849eb2c3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:67af0e01d0f7f873133b8c9360b96e7ef47de4ade3d6922e529b1153e278a022", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0005>.\nLet <MATH_0006> be an <MATH_0007>-invariant morphism of algebraic spaces over\n<MATH_0008>. Let <MATH_0009> be a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0010>\nand let <MATH_0011> be the base change as in\nLemma <REF_0001>. Then\n<MATH_0012>\nis a <MATH_0013>-fibre product of stacks in groupoids over <MATH_0014>.\nFor the construction of quotient stacks and the morphisms in this\ndiagram, see\nGroupoids in Spaces, Section <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b974b4c845e6b7019c37b0af65dc98bca745559026c78c5582f68c0a835bc82", "unit_id": "tag:0DTG:statement"}
